        "title": "Add Galician localization",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Add Galician (`gl`) as a selectable CodexBar app language with a complete 1,113-key catalog.\n- Add Galician website copy, locale detection, language-picker entry, and `hreflang` metadata.\n- Keep every existing locale's language picker current with `Galego`.\n- Reconstruct and complete the contribution from #1872 because its head branch does not allow maintainer edits.\n\n## Improvements over #1872\n\n- Fill the 164 app strings added since the contributor branch diverged from `main`.\n- Add exact English/Galician key-set parity regression coverage, representative translation checks, and required terminal-string checks.\n- Add the website locale and extend the site locale validator from 21 to 22 expected languages.\n- Add the maintainer changelog entry thanking @B1NAR10.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `plutil -lint` passes for every app localization catalog.\n- App locale checker reports 1,113/1,113 Galician keys with no missing or stale entries.\n- Site locale checker reports 22 locales and 139 messages per locale.\n- `swift test --filter LocalizationLanguageCatalogTests` passes 21 tests.\n- `make check` passes: site/app locale checks, 144 links, SwiftFormat, and SwiftLint across 1,245 files.\n- `make test` completes all 46 shards; one unrelated local shard passed on its automatic retry.\n- `./Scripts/package_app.sh` builds and signs the app plus widget bundle.\n- Real packaged-app proof under a disposable `HOME`, `CODEX_HOME`, `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, and config path with Keychain access process-disabled: Galician menu labels render, Settings renders without clipping, General shows `Idioma — Galego`, and the live language picker marks `Galego` selected.\n- Local website proof at `?lang=gl`: `html.lang=gl`, LTR direction, no i18n error marker, Galician title/hero/CTA, and a 22-option picker selecting `Galego`.\n- Autoreview: clean after completing the catalog and removing one stale key (confidence 0.93).\n\n## Risk\n\nLow and localized to translation/catalog registration. Key-set equality and locale validators prevent missing or extra app/site messages; packaged-app and website proof cover the runtime wiring.\n\n## Attribution\n\nThe implementation commit preserves Alberto Xosé Méndez Taboada as co-author.\n",
